<h1>TrackedEntityLayer</h1>
<p>High-performance real-time entity rendering with smooth animation, decorations, clustering, and interaction.</p>

<h2 id="train_tracking">// train_tracking</h2>
<p>This example simulates 47 trains across the Luxembourg rail network. Each train is a tracked entity whose position, rotation, and feature-state properties update every tick without re-creating the underlying MapLibre source.</p>

<p>Features demonstrated:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Declarative orchestration: hand <code>TrackedEntityLayer</code> your items plus selectors (<code>ItemId</code>, <code>Position</code>, <code>Icon</code>, <code>Rotation</code>, <code>Color</code>, <code>Properties</code>)</li>
    <li>Updates cross the interop boundary as binary motion frames and small structural diffs — never as a rebuilt feature collection</li>
    <li>Multi-layer <code>EntityDecoration</code> children with conditional display modes (always, on hover, on hover-or-select). For layers with thousands of entities, prefer <code>OnHover</code>/<code>OnHoverOrSelect</code> for text decorations — always-on labels double the symbol count the renderer must lay out per update.</li>
    <li>Zoom-to-dissolve clustering via the shared <code>ClusterOptions</code> model on the <code>Cluster</code> parameter</li>
    <li>Hover styling runs locally in JavaScript; selection binds to the <code>SelectedIds</code> parameter</li>
    <li>Smooth position interpolation via the <code>Animate</code> parameter</li>
    <li>SVG-to-data-URI custom icon registration via the map <code>Images</code> parameter</li>
    <li>Style composition with a railway overlay on a Positron base</li>
    <li>Interactive <a href="/components/controls#legend_map_controls">LegendMapControl</a> inside <code>MapControls</code>, with custom swatch templates</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="tracked_entity_clustering">// tracked_entity_clustering</h2>
<p><code>TrackedEntityLayer</code> uses the same <code>ClusterOptions</code> model as <code>GeoJsonSource</code>. Use <code>ClusterOptions.Default</code> for standard cluster circles and click-to-zoom behavior, or use <code>ClusterOptions.Create</code> when you need custom radius, max zoom, aggregate values, visuals, or click behavior.</p>
<p>The GeoJSON clustering section shows the same practical patterns for custom cluster layers, aggregate properties, custom rendering, and practical limits. Apply those patterns through the <code>Cluster</code> parameter; aggregate cluster properties read the values supplied by the <code>Properties</code> selector.</p>
<CodeBlock Language="razor" Files="@_trackedClusteringExamples" />

<ExampleView TComponent="TrainTrackingExample"
             AdditionalSources="@([typeof(TrainTrackingPresentation), typeof(TrainSampleSimulation)])">
    <TrainTrackingExample />
</ExampleView>

@code {
    private static readonly Dictionary<string, string> _trackedClusteringExamples = new()
    {
        ["DefaultTrackedEntityClustering.razor"] = """
            <TrackedEntityLayer TItem="Train"
                                Id="trains"
                                Items="@_trains"
                                ItemId="@(train => train.Id)"
                                Position="@(train => train.Position)"
                                IconImage="train-icon"
                                Cluster="@ClusterOptions.Default" />

            @code {
                private IReadOnlyList<Train> _trains = [];

                protected override void OnInitialized() => _trains = LoadTrains();
            }
            """,
        ["CustomTrackedEntityClusters.razor"] = """
            @code {
                private static readonly ClusterOptions _trainClusters = ClusterOptions.Create(
                    radius: 64,
                    maxZoom: 12,
                    minPoints: 2,
                    properties: new Dictionary<string, object>
                    {
                        ["internationalPresence"] = new object[] { "max", new object[] { "get", "internationalPresence" } },
                    },
                    layerSet: ClusterLayerSet.Custom(
                        ClusterLayerDefinition.Circle(
                            "cluster-halo",
                            color: "#f97316",
                            radius: Expr.Step("point_count", 28, 10, 36, 50, 44),
                            opacity: 0.22),
                        ClusterLayerDefinition.Circle(
                            "clusters",
                            color: Expr.Step("internationalPresence", "#2563eb", 1, "#dc2626"),
                            radius: Expr.Step("point_count", 18, 10, 24, 50, 30),
                            strokeColor: "#ffffff",
                            strokeWidth: 2),
                        ClusterLayerDefinition.Symbol(
                            "cluster-count",
                            textField: Expr.Get("point_count_abbreviated"),
                            textColor: "#ffffff",
                            textSize: 13)),
                    clickBehavior: ClusterClickBehavior.ZoomToDissolve);

            }

            <TrackedEntityLayer TItem="Train"
                                Id="trains"
                                Items="@_trains"
                                ItemId="@(train => train.Id)"
                                Position="@(train => train.Position)"
                                IconImage="train-icon"
                                Properties="@(train => new Dictionary<string, object?>
                                {
                                    ["internationalPresence"] = train.IsInternational ? 1 : 0,
                                })"
                                Cluster="@_trainClusters" />
            """,
    };
}
